# `.forge/orientation.md` is generated by `orientation_body` in
# packages/runner/crates/forge-runner-core/src/workspace/orientation.rs, and
# `this_repo_committed_orientation_matches_the_generator` compares the committed file
# byte for byte against that Rust literal, which is LF. A checkout that converts to CRLF
# — Git for Windows sets core.autocrlf=true by default, and the Windows CI runner
# inherits it — makes every line compare equal and only the total length differ, so the
# test fails reporting `the two differ in length only` and names drift that is not there.
# The invariant is that the committed file matches the generator; the line endings a
# checkout hands us are not part of it.
.forge/orientation.md eol=lf
